      en: ["Named after Moka, the King of the Bubi (died 1898).", "Situated in the Moka Valley at roughly 1,400m altitude.", "Primary hub for primate research on Bioko Island.", "Home to the sacred volcanic crater lake, Lake Moka.", "Known for the production of potatoes and cabbage.", "Considered the coldest inhabited settlement in Equatorial Guinea."],
